  "notes": "{寄|よ}る has two main meanings: to physically approach something, or to briefly stop at a place.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{寄|よ}せる→寄せる：02329_yoseru⟧ (transitive, to bring near)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{寄|よ}っている indicates the state of being near or having stopped by.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{寄|よ}る: to stop by (a place)\n- {寄|よ}って⟦くる→来る：00254_kuru⟧: to approach, come near\n- {寄|よ}って⟦いく→行く：00119_iku⟧: to stop by on the way\n- ⟦{帰|かえ}り→帰り：01275_kaeri⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{寄|よ}る: to stop by on the way home\n\nUSAGE:\nDo not confuse with ⟦{因|よ}る→よる：09857_yoru⟧ (to be due to) or ⟦{拠|よ}る→よる：09857_yoru⟧ (to be based on), which use different kanji.",
